{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/761660-creating-beasts-out-of-monsters-with-histories","id":761660,"title":"Creating Beasts out of Monsters With Histories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-09T12:26:52-08:00","id":761660,"title":"Creating Beasts out of Monsters With Histories","content":"So one of the things that drew me to Beast in the first place was the thought of playing a mythological monster. Of reversing the normal narrative and turning the thing that the Hero slays as part of his journey into the player character. But the current rules don't seem to support that. Right now, despite the lack of a humanity stat, the context of Beasts is still very much, &quot;You were born and lived a human life until you were devoured, you retain your old memories and the mindset they shaped, modified only by your new urges, etc, etc.&quot; Except I don't actually want to play a human who was Devoured. I want to play the monster that ate the human (that killed the rat that ate the malt that lay in the house that Jack built). <br /> <br /> I guess what I want to know is, is there any way to support this kind of character in the game as it stands right now? A thing that rose out of the darkness of sixty centuries, out of a legacy of hunger, blood, and fear that poured itself into human form to better walk among its prey. Perhaps a Beast that was once an actual, honest to goodness dragon now bound in human flesh. Maybe a Beast who of old stalked the land as a naagloshii or something similar that found a way to escape the limitations of its native condition through the Devouring. Or one that remembers having been a servant of Nemesis herself, dispensing retribution upon mortals whose hubris provoked her lady. Or one who is very much like Illyria from Angel. Can this be done? How would you handle the creature's actual memories of its previous existence: The actual history, the background of that monster and where it came from? Just make them such that most of them aren't relevant to its day to day existence, and it has to depend on the memories of its human shell? Or is there another WoD game line that would better represent such a creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T13:30:26-08:00","id":761680,"title":"","content":"There's a section in the Kickstarter that talks about Horrors with a past- they are goetic beings, after all, and the 'ghost' of a Beast is usually an Unfettered Horror. Mage's Secrets of the Ruined Temple mentions them long before Beast was a thing, the idea of these Astral mythical creatures possessing or even Claiming a human.<br /> <br /> Here's the quote from Chapter Two: <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">&quot;Most Horrors are ancient. Their roots lie in the earliest epoch of human history, when these hairless, defenseless apes lived in terror of predators, uncaring elements, and plagues for which they had no names. Over time they become encrusted in myth and legend; the natural human response to a recurring nightmare in their midst. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Rarely, a Beast inherits a strong Horror with a name and sense of history. She awakens with a mythic identity overlaid upon her human self. She is not just Ugallu. She is Ashalla, the Idiptu wind-fiend who unleashed hell on ancient Babylon. She feels compelled to walk among its ruins, even though she is also Ashya Dochev from Kazan, Russia. &quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So it appears as though there is a precedent for Beasts believing they are the reincarnations of the Horrors, rather than a human with a Horror. That, I suppose, is the point of the Legend, and when they become the Beast Incarnate, it becomes the source of their Myth. I can totally believe that some Incarnate Beasts with a true sense of history became that way by replaying the myths they came from, only <i>this </i>time they subvert the narrative they were born of and triumph over the Hero. Maybe there are even Beasts who believe they deserve priority and seniority over other Beasts because their Horrors come with a name and a history.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:02:55-08:00","id":761700,"title":"","content":"Ah, cool. I hadn't seen that particular section of the text <br /> But there's no mechanical support for this? No way to represent the memories of your mythic identity, or any connections it might have with beings that could still be around? <br /> <br /> Well, I suppose you could try to represent that with the actual allies and connection background... maybe your Horror has been reborn a number of times, and in each of those lives you have been friends with the same Mummy, which could justify taking said mummy as an ally? Would it work to represent old contacts from the time your Horror was incarnate in a human body back in the 60's (but died before you were born) with the contacts background? Still no way to easily do its memories, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:14:13-08:00","id":762054,"title":"","content":"There are still questions to be asked about the whole mythic identity thing, though.<br /> <br /> What kind of beings qualify for use as horrors with mythic identities? Should this be kept to monsters, or are gods and/or their servants fair game, too? Could a Nemesis actually be *Nemesis* herself? Should territory already claimed by another supernatural splat be avoided, or would it be totally fine to have Samael or Lucifer as your Horror, or Azazel or Mephistopheles? I assume J\u00f6tnar are fair game for Anakim. What sort of thing is kosher? What isn't? Is the truth of the claim less important than your ability to back up the <i>legend</i>? Guidelines would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:40:18-08:00","id":762343,"title":"","content":"Seems to me that this is simply the type of thing you could role-play. The player simply buys appropriate skills and attributes as they &quot;remember&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T21:54:41-08:00","id":763752,"title":"","content":"If you want rules for it, I'd suggest adopting residual memory from Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:04:53-08:00","id":763760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/761660-creating-beasts-out-of-monsters-with-histories?p=762054#post762054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of beings qualify for use as horrors with mythic identities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess some level of Advanced Fame is practically a necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}